-- title:
--   Ramification index one along α_H at formally unramified points
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M \neq 0$ with $p \mid M$ and $M/p \neq 0$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbf{Z}/M)^\times$, and assume the $q$-series `jqModC ℚ` lies in `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`, the subfield of $\mathbf{Q}((q))$ generated by ratios of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbf{Z})$. Let $\mathfrak{X}$ be an inhabitant of `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`, the structure packaging an integral, proper, flat model `X p (ΓM M H) hj` over `R p` with normal affine sections, a smooth proper model at level `ΓN p M H hpM`, a curve model $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}$ over $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ of $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}\cdot F(\Gamma_H(M))$ (the intermediate field `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` obtained by adjoining to $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ the coefficientwise images of `xHFunctionField M H`), an isomorphism $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{eeta}$ of its curve onto the base change of the model along $R_p \to \overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ compatible with the structure maps, a Galois-equivariance clause, and a pinning of the finite chart by $q$-expansions. Let $\alpha_H$ be an $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$-algebra map from `xHFunctionFieldBar (M / p) (infSubgroup p M H hpM)` — the level-$(M/p)$ field for the image of $H$ under `ZMod.unitsMap` — into `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` which leaves underlying Laurent series unchanged and is integral. Let `Meta₀` be a curve model of that level-$(M/p)$ field over $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$: an integral scheme, proper and smooth of relative dimension $1$ over $\operatorname{Spec} \overline{\mathbf{Q}}$, with a ring isomorphism of the field onto its function field over the base, together with a bijection from closed points to places matching stalks with valuation subrings, and with every finite set of points contained in an affine open. Let `eeta₀` be an isomorphism from `Meta₀.C` onto the base change along $R_p \to \overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ of `toBase p (ΓN p M H hpM) hj` with `eeta₀ ≫ pullback.snd = Meta₀.toBase`, such that the preimage of the image of the finite chart `ιFin` is nonempty and such that, for every element $a$ of `chartAlgFin p (ΓN p M H hpM) hj`, the function-field element obtained from $a$ by transport through `eeta₀` followed by `pullback.fst`, germ at the generic point and `Meta₀.ffEquiv.symm`, has as underlying Laurent series the coefficientwise image under `coeffEmb` of the $q$-expansion of $a$. Finally let $y$ be a $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$-point of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.C$, that is a section of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.\mathrm{toBase}$, let $V$ be an open of `X p (ΓM M H) hj` containing the image of the closed point of $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ under $y$ followed by $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{eeta}$ and `pullback.fst`, and assume the inclusion of $V$ followed by the underlying morphism `𝔛.π.1` of the degeneracy datum carried by $\mathfrak{X}$ is formally unramified. Then the place of `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` attached to $y$ by the bijection `𝔛.Meta.pointEquivPlace` has ramification index $1$ along $\alpha_H$: the least $n > 0$ for which some nonzero $f$ in the level-$(M/p)$ field satisfies $\operatorname{ord}(\alpha_H f) = n$ equals $1$.
--
--   This is the statement that the degeneracy embedding of function fields is unramified at those geometric points of the generic fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model at which the level-lowering morphism is formally unramified; it specialises the general curve-model criterion [`AlgebraicCurve.CurveModel.ramificationIndexAlong_pointEquivPlace_eq_one_of_formallyUnramified`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.CurveModel.ramificationIndexAlong_pointEquivPlace_eq_one_of_formallyUnramified) using the identification of the generic function-field map provided by [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.fromSpecStalk_genericPoint_comp_eq_specMap_ffEquiv_degeneracyEmb_of_chartPin`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.fromSpecStalk_genericPoint_comp_eq_specMap_ffEquiv_degeneracyEmb_of_chartPin). It feeds the multiplicity bookkeeping for divisor pull-back along $\alpha_H$ used in the Jacobian and Picard-group computations at level $M$ and $M/p$.
-- source:
